# Build context for every per-service Dockerfile is src/backend (the backend root),
# because each service references the shared building-blocks project next to it.
# Without this file the context is ~2.1 GB of host build artifacts, which is sent
# to the daemon once per service and starves the Docker VM during a parallel build.
#
# The Dockerfiles restore and publish inside the image, so host build output is
# never needed — and copying it in can poison the container build with artifacts
# compiled for a different RID.

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Test results / coverage
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx
**/coverage*.xml

# NOTE: appsettings.*.json is deliberately NOT excluded. gateway/Gateway/
# appsettings.Development.json is tracked and carries YARP cluster config, and the
# containers run with ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development. docker-compose environment
# variables override those values, but dropping the files would still be a change to
# the deploy image, not just a context trim.

# User/IDE cruft
**/*.user
**/*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
.DS_Store
